\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Once to every man and nation
\par Comes the moment to decide,
\par In the strife of truth with falsehood,
\par For the good or evil side;
\par Some great cause, God's new Messiah,
\par Offering each the bloom or blight-
\par And the choice goes by for ever
\par "Twixt that darkness and that light.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Then to side with truth is noble,
\par When we share her wretched crust,
\par Ere her cause bring frame and profit,
\par And 'tis prosperous to be just;
\par Then it is the brave man chooses,
\par While the coward stands aside,
\par Till the multitude make virtue
\par Of the faith they had denied.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. By the light of burning martyrs,
\par Christ, Thy bleeding feet we track
\par Tolling up new Calvaries ever
\par With the Cross that turns not back.
\par New occassions teach new duties;
\par Time makes ancient good uncouth;
\par They must upward still and onward
\par Who would keep abreast of truth.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Thou the cause of evil prosper,
\par Yet 'tis truth alone is strong;
\par Thou her portion be the scaffold,
\par And upon the throne be wrong-
\par Yet that scaffold sways the future,
\par And, behind the dim unknown,
\par Standeth God within the shadow,
\par Keeping watch above His own.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

